            <ArticleTitle>Resolution of exercise intolerance secondary to ischemic sinus node dysfunction following percutaneous transluminal angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>44-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on a case of significant exertional symptoms secondary to occlusion of a nondominant right coronary artery proximal to the sino-atrial branch, with associated exercise-induced sinus node dysfunction. Successful angioplasty of the occluded right coronary artery restored a normal functional capacity and sinus tachycardia response to exercise.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
